# Components

Colocate each feature as `index.tsx` + `styles.css.ts` + `hooks/useX.ts`. Optional: `types.d.ts` / `types.ts`, `context/`, nested `components/`.

```tsx
// ✅ presentational component + hook for data
export const Experiences = () => {
  const { t, experiences } = useExperiences();
  return (
    <section id="experience" className={Container}>
      <h2 className={Title}>{t('experience:title')}</h2>
      {experiences.map(({ id }) => (
        <p key={id}>{t(`experience:${id}.role`)}</p>
      ))}
    </section>
  );
};
```

- Named exports, functional components. Keep `import React from 'react'` if the file already uses it.
- Hooks own **structure** (ids, urls, icons, numeric scores). Locale JSON owns **copy**.
- Section roots use `<section id="…">` matching menu hashes (`#about`, `#experience`, …).
- Conditional UI: `@components/shared/When`. Two-column wrap: `@components/shared/Row`.
- Emphasize terms in translated text with `@utils/highlight` `Highlight`, not manual `<strong>` splits.
- Ambient `types.d.ts` (no import/export) is the local default; `LangSelector/types.ts` is the exception — match the folder.
